入组条件:
Inclusion Criteria:

1. Patients with suspected biliary tract carcinoma who are eligible for surgical exploration, with postoperative pathological confirmation of biliary tract adenocarcinoma;
2. Age 18-80 years;
3. Preoperative assessment indicating that the primary tumor is potentially amenable to R0/R1 resection;
4. Preoperative evidence of lymph node metastases with at least one of the following features indicating that complete surgical resection or lymph node dissection may not be feasible:

* Local invasion of regional lymph nodes, such that complete surgical resection may not be feasible;
* Retroperitoneal lymph node metastases extending beyond the feasible surgical dissection field;
5. Whole-body PET/CT demonstrating metastatic lymph node involvement confined to a contiguous extended lymphatic field that can be encompassed within a single radiotherapy plan, with the involved lymph nodes extending from the lower paraesophageal lymph node region superiorly to the lymph nodes at the level of the abdominal aortic bifurcation inferiorly;
6. No distant organ metastases, non-regional lymph node metastases, or intrahepatic metastatic lesions are allowed. Isolated right internal mammary lymph node or left supraclavicular lymph node involvement is permitted; however, these lesions will not be included in the initial radiotherapy field and may receive subsequent definitive local radiotherapy based on multidisciplinary evaluation and treatment response;
7. Prior systemic therapy, including chemotherapy, targeted therapy, or immunotherapy, is permitted. Prior local treatment, including interventional therapy or radiofrequency ablation, is not permitted;
8. Eastern Cooperative Oncology Group (ECOG) performance status of 0-2 and a life expectancy of \>3 months;
9. Child-Pugh class A5 or A6;
10. Liver function meeting the following criteria:

* ALT ≤2.5 × the upper limit of normal (ULN), with AST ≤6 × ULN when ALT ≤1.5 × ULN and AST ≤2.5 × ULN when ALT \>1.5 × ULN but ≤2.5 × ULN, after excluding AST elevation due to myocardial infarction;
* Total bilirubin (TBIL) \ 450 ms in males or \>470 ms in females);
12. Known HIV infection.

Inclusion Criteria:

* Patients that signed the formal consent;
* Previous history of head and neck squamous cell carcinoma with no more than three years of follow-up;
* History of squamous cell carcinoma in the following sub-sites: oral cavity, oropharynx, larynx and hypopharynx;
* Absence of active malignant disease (HNSCC) with at least three months of follow-up (without signs of residual disease, recurrence or second primary invasive tumors);
* Normal liver, hematologic and renal function.
* Eastern Cooperative Oncology Group (ECOG) Performance Status: 0, 1 or 2;
* Smoking history (current smokers or former smokers). Former users were defined as patients who had quit smoking at least one year prior to diagnosis and smoked more than 100 cigarettes in their lifetime.

Exclusion Criteria:

* Any active malignancy;
* History of invasive malignancies (other than HNSCC) diagnosed within the last 2 years (controlled non-melanoma skin cancer are an exception);
* History of hepatitis B, hepatitis C, HIV, chronic liver disease or chronic pancreatic disease;
* Any comorbid medical or psychiatric disorder that it is not well controlled;
* Patients under immunosuppression or under systemic corticosteroid therapy to treat any active autoimmune disease;
* Patients that still have documented toxicities greater than grade 1 (CTCEA NCI v4.0) due to the previously treated HNSCC;
* Patients that are pregnant or breast-feeding;
* Patients that are in routine use of the following medications due to drug interaction: phenytoin, carbamazepine, barbiturates, chlorpromazine, diazepam, clonazepam, lamotrigine, primidone, amitriptyline, nortriptyline, ethosuximide, warfarin, tolbutamide or topiramate;
* Any medical condition or mental disorder that can potentially increase their risk during the trial (e.g. epilepsy, active infection, schizophrenia);
* Patients that are already under valproic acid use due to neurological or psychiatric disorders;
* Patients that are allergic/intolerant to valproic acid;
* Patients with alcoholism history within the past year or that was under alcoholism treatment in the same period;
* Institutionalized patients.

干预:
DRUG: prescribing anapproved drug, examination

* Blood test to assess serum zonulin levels;
* Esophagogastroduodenoscopyand colonoscopy with biopsy from the small and large intestine followed by histological examination;
