* Crisis: a serious, life-threatening, rapid worsening of MG requiring intubation or noninvasive ventilation to avoid intubation.
* Impending crisis: rapid clinical worsening of MG that, in the opinion of the treating physician, could lead to crisis in the short term (days to weeks) with blood gases suggest hypoxia (oxygen saturation \ 50mmHg).

